VERDICT: The entire h5df-format subsystem is MISSING in dafr - this is a whole missing storage format, not a narrowing. dafr v0.4.4 has no `.h5df`/`.h5dfs` reader or writer; R/open_daf.R:37-38 hard-rejects those URIs with stop('H5df backend not supported yet'). The only HDF5 in dafr is h5ad/AnnData (h5ad_as_daf / daf_as_h5ad, R/anndata_format.R), which is a DIFFERENT format (the h5df .md and .jl both stress h5df is NOT h5ad-compatible: h5df_format.jl:5-9). dafr's native storage backends are memory_daf, files_daf, zarr_daf, and read-only http_daf.

IMPORTANT CONTEXT FOR TRIAGE: This gap is KNOWN AND INTENTIONALLY DEFERRED by the dafr authors, not a hidden bug. It is documented as reorder-parity divergence 'R3' (dev/notes/2026-05-07-reorder-jl-parity-divergences.md:77-86, marked 'Out of scope - not on the roadmap') and deferred across slice notes (slice-6-exit.md:67, slice-8-kickoff.md:87, slice-10-kickoff.md:30, 2026-04-22-slice-10-wrapper-parity-analysis.md). Parity tests explicitly skip() h5df with messages like 'dafr does not have an h5df backend' (test-reorder-jl-parity.R:162,367; test-data-jl-parity.R:302). So while it is the single largest feature gap in this subsystem (~2290 lines of Julia with no R counterpart, including the full Formats storage protocol, packed/compressed encoding, mmap zero-copy reads, sparse-string nztxt and Bool-all-true encodings, alignment enforcement, multi-DAF .h5dfs#/group scheme, and a crash-safe reorder protocol), it is graceful-fail (clean stop) rather than silent-wrong-answer, and it is well-acknowledged.

Julia public surface (h5df_format.jl + h5df_format.md): the single export is `H5df`; documented constants MAJOR_VERSION=1 / MINOR_VERSION=0 (jl:199/209); constructor H5df(root, mode='r'; name=nothing, packed=false) with root accepting path/HDF5.File/HDF5.Group; 4 modes (r/r+/w+/w) with documented create/truncate table; full Formats interface (scalars/axes/vectors/matrices has/set/get/delete/list + empty dense/sparse vector & matrix + relayout, jl:486-1570); Readers.is_leaf=true, complete_path; and the complete Reorder interface (lock/has_lock/backup/replace/cleanup/reset, jl:1641-2247). I deliberately did NOT enumerate trivially-derived overloads separately; julia_public_items_count=8 reflects the 8 distinct user-facing capabilities I filed under missing_in_r. All 7 probes are runnable Julia snippets paired with the dafr error they hit; none can produce an R round-trip because the backend is absent."}
